EDCH — attribution
==========================

Elite Dangerous game data
-------------------------
EDCH was created using assets and imagery from Elite Dangerous, with the
permission of Frontier Developments plc, for non-commercial purposes. It is not
endorsed by nor reflects the views or opinions of Frontier Developments and no
employee of Frontier Developments was involved in the making of it.

Community data used to build public/data/game.json (tools/gen_data.py)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
- dseelinger/d47 (MIT) — generated tables Materials.tsv, Blueprints.tsv,
  Engineers.tsv and fixed farming site positions, vendored in tools/sources/d47
  with their LICENSE and the commit they come from.
- msarilar/EDEngineer (MIT) — recipes and material origins, via d47.
- Elite Dangerous Almanac (Almanac-Core, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Elite Dangerous Community) — the game's own
  localized names (commodities, materials, Odyssey items, modules, blueprints, experimental effects),
  vendored in tools/sources/almanac with its LICENSE, ATTRIBUTIONS.md and the commit they come from.
- msarilar/EDEngineer (MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 Max) — translations of the game's names (materials, modules, blueprints), kept in tools/sources/edengineer/ and completed in tools/game_terms_*.txt.
- EDCD/EDDI (Apache License 2.0) — translations of the minor faction states (tools/game_terms_2.txt), and
  of the ranks and some commodities used in the engineers' requirements (public/locales/*.json,
  engineerData), from its DataDefinitions resources.
- EDCD/FDevIDs — journal symbols and grades, via d47.
- EDCD/coriolis-data — cross-check of recipes, via d47; Frame Shift Drive constants (optimal mass, max fuel
  per jump, fuel multiplier and power) in src/fsdData.ts, from modules/standard/frame_shift_drive.json.
  Game data © Frontier Developments plc, under its terms.

